  "evidencia": "Page: Roger Miller. Sentence: Roger Dean Miller, Sr. (January 2, 1936 – October 25, 1992) was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor, best known for his honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs. His most recognized tunes included the chart-topping country and pop hits \"King of the Road\", \"Dang Me\", and \"England Swings\", all from the mid-1960s Nashville sound era.\nPage: King of the Road (song). Sentence: \"King of the Road\" is a song written and originally recorded in November 1964 by country singer Roger Miller.\nPage: Do-Wacka-Do. Sentence: \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\" is a song, released in 1965, by American country music artist Roger Miller.\nPage: I Told You So: The Ultimate Hits of Randy Travis. Sentence: Travis' cover of Roger Miller's \"King of the Road\" is also included along with two tracks from his previous album \"Around the Bend\".",
