        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "70907e5a-49ed-55ec-9bf8-bdb56e6f7ace",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Miller, Randy Travis\n- Songs: \"King of the Road\", \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\"\n- Albums: I Told You So: The Ultimate Hits of Randy Travis, Around the Bend\n- Topics: country music, Nashville sound\n\nFacts:\n- Roger Miller was an American singer-songwriter, musician, and actor born on January 2, 1936, and he was best known for honky-tonk-influenced novelty songs.\n- Roger Miller wrote and originally recorded the song \"King of the Road\" in November 1964.\n- Roger Miller's most recognized mid-1960s Nashville sound-era hits included the chart-topping country and pop songs \"King of the Road\", \"Dang Me\", and \"England Swings\".\n- Roger Miller released the song \"(And You Had a) Do-Wacka-Do\" in 1965.\n- Randy Travis's album I Told You So: The Ultimate Hits of Randy Travis includes his cover of Roger Miller's \"King of the Road\" along with two tracks from Around the Bend.\n- Roger Miller died on October 25, 1992.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
